UID:delfina-gulbenkian-artists-portugal-lusophone-africa-2027@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T140457Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Delfina Foundation x Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation: Open
  Call for Artists from Portugal and Portuguese-Speaking African Nations (L
 ondon residency)
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation (UK Bran
 ch)\, Delfina Foundation welcomes applications from contemporary visual ar
 tists from Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-Bissau\, Cape Verde and
  Sao Tome and Principe for a London residency from 28 June to 17 September
  2027\, during Delfina's open summer season dedicated to independent resea
 rch. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be born in one of the six eligible count
 ries (individuals currently based in the UK are not eligible)\; be seeking
  to develop their practice through research\; be able to explain how an in
 ternational residency may benefit their career development and local netwo
 rks\; and be proficient in English (the interview is conducted in English)
 . Collectives and duos are advised to put forth one member to be in reside
 nce. THE PROGRAMME: alongside time and space to develop their work\, resid
 ents get guided visits to museums\, galleries\, non-profits\, artist-run s
 paces and studios\, plus trips to institutions outside London\; opportunit
 ies to meet artists\, curators\, academics and researchers through organis
 ed presentations\, studio visits\, events and meals\; professional develop
 ment including presentations and crits\, portfolio reviews and mentoring\;
  and collaborative exchange between residents through informal gatherings 
 and meals. APPLY via the online application form (Cognito Forms\, save-and
 -resume supported)\; Delfina strongly recommends reading the Guidance Note
 s document carefully before starting. All applicants notified by mid-Novem
 ber 2026. Deadline Sunday 4 October 2026\, 23:59 BST.\n\nOrganisation: Del
 fina Foundation\, in partnership with the Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation (
 UK Branch)\nLocation: Delfina Foundation\, 29-31 Catherine Place\, London\
 , UK. Applicants must be born in Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-B
 issau\, Cape Verde or Sao Tome and Principe\; individuals currently based 
 in the UK are not eligible.\nAward: Twelve-week fully funded residency: a 
 return economy-class flight\, airport transfers in the UK\, reimbursement 
 of visa fees if required\, a living allowance of GBP 40 per day\, a materi
 als budget of GBP 1\,200\, a travel pass for London's public transport net
 work\, and a single bedroom with a desk at Delfina Foundation\, a house ho
 sting up to eight residents with shared bathrooms\, laundry rooms\, kitche
 n\, library and dining room. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve weeks\,
  28 June to 17 September 2027\, during Delfina's open summer 2027 residenc
 y season.\n\nMore: https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/op
 en-call-for-artists-from-portugal-or-portugese-speaking-african-nations/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/open-call-for-arti
 sts-from-portugal-or-portugese-speaking-african-nations/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Delfina Foundation\, 29-31 Catherine Place\, London\, UK. Applican
 ts must be born in Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-Bissau\, Cape V
 erde or Sao Tome and Principe\; individuals currently based in the UK are 
 not eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shape-arts-emergent-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T140457Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Shape Arts: Emergent Residency 2026/27 (Tate St Ives / Po
 rthmeor Studios)
DESCRIPTION:Shape Arts' Emergent Residency places an early-career disabled 
 artist at Porthmeor Studios in St Ives\, in partnership with Tate St Ives.
  SUPPORT: GBP 3\,000 bursary and a one-week residency (18 to 24 January 20
 27\, plus travel days)\; a wider shortlisted cohort of disabled artists re
 ceives mentoring and support. ELIGIBILITY: self-identify as disabled\; age
 d 18+\; within the first five years of your artistic career (career pauses
  allowed)\; not in full-time education\; not previously shortlisted for Em
 ergent. The bursary and residency are only for artists who live or work in
  Cornwall\, Devon or Somerset\; disabled artists elsewhere in the UK can a
 pply for the shortlisted cohort. APPLICATION: via Google Form\, or a Word 
 form by email\; FAQs available in text\, audio\, BSL and Easy Read formats
 . DEADLINE: 1 November 2026\, 23:59.\n\nOrganisation: Shape Arts\, with Ta
 te St Ives\nLocation: Porthmeor Studios\, St Ives\, Cornwall\, UK. Residen
 cy bursary only for artists who live or work in Cornwall\, Devon or Somers
 et\; disabled artists elsewhere in the UK can apply for the shortlisted co
 hort.\nAward: GBP 3\,000 bursary for the selected residency artist (restri
 cted to artists living or working in Cornwall\, Devon or Somerset). Disabl
 ed artists in the rest of the UK can join the shortlisted cohort\, which b
 rings mentoring and profile but no stated bursary. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: One-week residency\, 18 to 24 January 2027\, plus travel days.\n\n
 More: https://www.shapearts.org.uk/Blog/apply-to-our-emergent-residency-pr
 ogramme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.shapearts.org.uk/Blog/apply-to-our-emergent-residency-progr
 amme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Porthmeor Studios\, St Ives\, Cornwall\, UK. Residency bursary onl
 y for artists who live or work in Cornwall\, Devon or Somerset\; disabled 
 artists elsewhere in the UK can apply for the shortlisted cohort.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gasworks-residency-artists-based-in-the-baltics-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T140457Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270203
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gasworks Residency 2027 for Artists Based in the Baltics 
 (London\, with Upe Foundation\; solo show 2028)
DESCRIPTION:Gasworks and the Upe Foundation offer a fully funded eleven-wee
 k London residency for one contemporary visual artist at a pivotal stage i
 n their career who is based in Lithuania\, Latvia or Estonia\, as part of 
 a multi-year partnership for artists and curators connected to the Baltic 
 region. The resident develops their practice in London from 7 July to 21 S
 eptember 2027 and returns for a solo exhibition at Gasworks in July to Sep
 tember 2028\, developed with the Upe Foundation Curatorial Fellow. WHAT YO
 U GET: a private studio at Gasworks\, accommodation in the Gasworks reside
 ncy house\, economy return flights and taxi transfers\, all visa costs and
  application support\, a weekly living stipend of GBP 175\, a materials bu
 dget of up to GBP 800\, studio visits and curatorial support. APPLICATION:
  read the Application Guidelines and Residency FAQ\, then submit via the o
 nline form on the call page. DEADLINE: 2 February 2027\, 13:00 UK time.\n\
 nOrganisation: Gasworks (London)\, with Upe Foundation\nLocation: London\,
  UK. For contemporary visual artists based in Lithuania\, Latvia or Estoni
 a.\nAward: Fully funded 11-week residency: weekly stipend of GBP 175\, mat
 erials budget up to GBP 800\, private studio\, accommodation\, economy ret
 urn flights and transfers\, all visa costs\, plus a solo exhibition at Gas
 works in 2028. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 11 weeks\, 7 July 
 to 21 September 2027\, followed by a solo exhibition at Gasworks in July t
 o September 2028.\n\nMore: https://gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/residency
 -open-call-for-artists-based-in-the-baltics-2027?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/residency-open-call-for-artists-b
 ased-in-the-baltics-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For contemporary visual artists based in Lithuania\, 
 Latvia or Estonia.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cove-park-awarded-residencies-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T140457Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cove Park Awarded Residencies 2027-2028 (Scotland\, UK\, 
 Central and South America and diasporas)
DESCRIPTION:Cove Park's biennial call for fully funded Awarded Residencies 
 at its 50-acre rural residency site in Argyll\, on the west coast of Scotl
 and\, programmed between May 2027 and December 2028. Residencies run from 
 2 weeks up to 12 weeks (average four weeks) and can be split across the tw
 o years around caring or work commitments\; international residents can co
 unt slow-travel time as part of the funded period. Open to artists\, creat
 ive practitioners\, writers\, translators and researchers in all art forms
  and at every career stage\, including collectives and collaborative group
 s\; no formal qualification needed. Priorities include work responding to 
 climate breakdown\, sound artists and musicians (new Sound Studio)\, and w
 ork on home\, place\, language (Scots\, Gaelic\, BSL)\, displacement and b
 elonging. No final presentation is required. ELIGIBILITY: based in the UK\
 , Central America or South America\; Central and South American diaspora a
 rtists based in Europe or North America\; or born in Scotland and living e
 lsewhere. Anyone in full- or part-time formal education on 11 December 202
 6 is not eligible. SUPPORT: GBP 775 per week fee\; travel allowance (Scotl
 and GBP 65 to 100 Central Belt\, up to GBP 200 Borders/Highlands/Islands\;
  rest of UK up to GBP 250\; Europe up to GBP 400\; other international up 
 to GBP 1\,250)\; materials up to GBP 150\; visa support\; private self-cat
 ering accommodation (suitable for collaborators and those attending with c
 hildren) and private studios. An Application Access Bursary (e.g. to pay a
  support worker) is available for applicants facing barriers due to disabi
 lity or neurodivergence\; request it from Alex Marrs by 30 November 2026. 
 Video or audio applications accepted. Applicants are asked not to use gene
 rative AI in their application. APPLY via the online form: 500-word statem
 ent\, 100-word bio\, CV\, up to 8 images or video/audio links or writing s
 amples. SELECTION: shortlisting by the programme team and former residents
 \; shortlist notified by 12 February 2027\; Zoom interviews the week of 22
  February 2027. Contact: Alex Marrs\, alex@covepark.org. DEADLINE: Friday 
 11 December 2026\, 5pm GMT.\n\nOrganisation: Cove Park\nLocation: Cove Par
 k\, Peaton Hill\, Argyll and Bute\, Scotland (in person\, private self-cat
 ering accommodation and studio). Open to people based in the UK\, Central 
 or South America\, Central and South American diaspora artists based in Eu
 rope or North America\, and Scotland-born artists living anywhere. Student
 s in formal education are not eligible.\nAward: Fully funded: GBP 775 per 
 week fee (VAT inclusive\, freelance)\, travel allowance (Scotland GBP 65 t
 o 200\, rest of UK up to GBP 250\, Europe up to GBP 400\, other internatio
 nal up to GBP 1\,250)\, materials up to GBP 150 for studio-based practitio
 ners\, private accommodation and studio\, visa and access support. Applica
 tion Access Bursary available (request by 30 November 2026). No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: 2 to 12 weeks (average 4)\, between May 2027 and Decembe
 r 2028\n\nMore: https://covepark.org/awarded-residencies-2027-2028/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://covepark.org/awarded-residencies-2027-2028/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cove Park\, Peaton Hill\, Argyll and Bute\, Scotland (in person\, 
 private self-catering accommodation and studio). Open to people based in t
 he UK\, Central or South America\, Central and South American diaspora art
 ists based in Europe or North America\, and Scotland-born artists living a
 nywhere. Students in formal education are not eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eastside-projects-radical-sabbatical-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T140457Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Deadline: Radical Sabbatical 2027: six-month residencies on touch a
 t the University of Birmingham (GBP 3\,500 fee + GBP 500 production\, UK-b
 ased artists)
DESCRIPTION:Radical Sabbatical is a collaboration between Eastside Projects
  and University Collections at the University of Birmingham that gives two
  artists a six-month residency centred on research and development. The 20
 27 edition is themed around touch: artists are matched with one or more ac
 ademics and asked to interrogate and interpret academic research\, with ar
 eas including digital touch and technology\, haptic and sensory experience
 \, embodied knowledge\, disability and inclusive design\, medical perspect
 ives\, materiality and craft\, memory and emotion\, and human and non-huma
 n sensory connection. Academic partners include the Active Touch Lab and t
 he Department of Creative Industries. Artists have regular one-to-one conv
 ersations with staff and present at a final sharing event. ELIGIBILITY: ar
 tists based in the UK. SUPPORT: GBP 3\,500 artist fee plus GBP 500 product
 ion budget. TIMELINE: deadline Friday 20 November 2026\, 11:59pm\; intervi
 ews for shortlisted artists 10 December 2026\; residencies begin January 2
 027\; final sharing event and evaluation June/July 2027. APPLY using the a
 rtists' callout pack linked from the call page\; questions to info@eastsid
 eprojects.org.\n\nOrganisation: Eastside Projects with University Collecti
 ons\, University of Birmingham\nLocation: University of Birmingham\, Birmi
 ngham\, UK (in person\, research residency). Open to artists based in the 
 UK only.\nAward: GBP 3\,500 artist fee plus GBP 500 production budget per 
 artist\; two artists selected.\nDuration: 6 months\, January to June/July 
 2027\n\nMore: https://eastsideprojects.org/projects/apply-now-radical-sabb
 atical-2027-residencies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://eastsideprojects.org/projects/apply-now-radical-sabbatical-2027
 -residencies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:University of Birmingham\, Birmingham\, UK (in person\, research r
 esidency). Open to artists based in the UK only.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
